README for shasta 1.0.0  --  3 September 2002

This is version 1.0.0 of the shasta interactive server.
Shasta provides you with interactive access to selected
functionalities of Sum^it. You do not need Aldor to use shasta.

Downloading shasta 1.0.0:
-------------------------
You must get both the platform-independent shasta.tar.gz file
and the executable corresponding to the desired operating system
and processor:
-  shasta-1.0.0.gmp4.1_ev5.gz   for DEC/OSF1 on an EV5 processor
-  shasta-1.0.0.gmp4.1_ev6.gz   for DEC/OSF1 on an EV6 processor
-  shasta-1.0.0.gmp4.1_p1.gz    for Linux on an Intel Pentium processor
-  shasta-1.0.0.gmp4.1_p2.gz    for Linux on an Intel Pentium2 processor
-  shasta-1.0.0.gmp4.1_p3.gz    for Linux on an Intel Pentium3 processor

Installing shasta 1.0.0:
------------------------
- issue 'tar -xvzf shasta.tar.gz' to install the platform-independent parts
- move the shasta executable into the bin subdirectory of shasta and unzip it
- check the shasta user guide in shasta/share/doc for further instructions.

Please report any bugs or problems you encounter to   sumit@sophia.inria.fr
We would be thankful if you could send an email notification to the above
address after installing shasta, so we can keep track of who uses shasta.
Simply put 'shasta 1.0.0' in the subject line.

